  "answer": "I can't give you a reliable peso rate. None of my data sources carry the Argentine peso (ARS). The RBA's exchange rate table, which I checked, covers about two dozen currencies but not ARS, and the ABS search returned nothing.\n\nHere is what I can give you. The RBA's latest AUD/USD rate is **0.6947 US dollars per A$1** (16 October 2026). To get pesos, multiply that by the current official ARS/USD rate, which you can find on the Banco Central de la República Argentina (BCRA) website or a bank or currency site such as XE. Note that Argentina has had several exchange rates (official, banks, and informal \"blue\" or MEP rates), and they can differ noticeably, so check which one you need.",
